quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  21,25,"We never sent any messenger before you, but We revealed to him: ‘There is no god except Me.’ So worship Me."
  21,26,"And they say: ‘The Most-Compassionate (Lord) has taken (angels as His) children.’ Glory be to Him. Instead, they are (His) honoured servants."
  21,27,"They do not precede Him in speech, but they act by His command."
  21,28,"He knows what is before them and what is behind them, and they do not intercede except for him with whom He is pleased. And they (themselves) are apprehensive in fear of Him."
  21,29,"Whosoever among them says, ‘I am a god besides Him’, we shall reward such (a person) with Hell. That is how We recompense the wrongdoers."
  21,30,"Have the disbelievers not considered that the heavens and the earth were joined together (at one time), and then We split them apart? And We originated (the life of) all living organisms (on earth) from water. Will they still not believe (after learning these facts mentioned in the Qur’an)?"
  21,31,"And We set firm mountains in the earth, lest it should shake with them (while rotating in its orbit). And We made on this (earth) broad ways so that they might find routes (to different destinations)."
  21,32,We made the upper spheres of the earth a secure roof.* Yet they are disregardful of its signs.
  21,33,"He is the One Who created the night and the day, the sun and the moon—each moving in an orbit."
  21,34,"And We have not granted eternity to any human before you (in this world). So, if you die, will they live forever?"
  21,35,"Every soul is sure to taste death, and We try you (all) with evil and with good as a test. And to Us shall you be returned."
